  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 143 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nA stronger cold front will move through the area Sunday afternoon\ninto Sunday night. This will result in much cooler highs on \nMonday and Tuesday in the low to mid 50s, with mostly cloudy \nskies. No precipitation is expected from Monday through Wednesday.\nAdditional broad upper level troughing will move into the western\nU. S. by the second half of this week, bringing southwesterly \nflow into our area. Southerly low level flow, bringing Gulf \nmoisture back into the region, combined with shortwave energy \nmoving over the area in southwesterly flow will bring our next \nlow(20%) chance for precipitation Thursday into next weekend. \nTemperatures are expected to warm back up into the upper 60s to \naround 70 by next Thursday and Friday.",
